meta {
  name: Find Hardware for WorkspaceID
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/devices?workspaceId={{workspaceid}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  workspaceId: {{workspaceid}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  ~Authorization: Bearer {{CDRToken}}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists all hardware devices registered to a specific Workspace (a physical space like a meeting
  room or hot desk), using the `workspaceId` query parameter on the List Devices endpoint.

  **Parameters**
  - `workspaceId` (query, required for this example) — the Workspace/Place ID to filter devices by.
    Bound to the collection variable `{{workspaceid}}` (see the collection-level docs), which is
    populated with a worked example. Swap it for a real Workspace ID from "List Workspaces" to try
    your own.

  **Usage**: Run "List Workspaces" first to find a `workspaceId`, then use it here to see every
  device assigned to that space (useful for shared/hot-desk areas rather than a single owned user).

  Note: this collection variable is named `workspaceid` (lowercase) to match the value already
  defined at the top level; an unused empty `workspaceId` (camelCase) variable also exists for
  ad-hoc testing with your own ID.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/devices/list-devices

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
